.DS_Store

# The Sparkle private key, if it is ever exported here. It must never be public.
slate-update-key.txt
*.private

# The DMG is committed on purpose: GitHub Pages serves whatever is in the repo,
# so the download button needs the file to be here. That is why there is no
# Slate-*.dmg line below. One held the first build back until it was notarized
# and came out when 1.1.0 shipped, so nothing here stops a bad DMG any more and
# the check is yours to do by hand. Only ever commit a build that came out of
# `scripts/notarize.sh` and passes:
#
#   xcrun stapler validate Slate-<version>.dmg
#   spctl -a -t open --context context:primary-signature -vv Slate-<version>.dmg
#
# A development-signed build would be blocked by Gatekeeper on every Mac but
# the one that made it, and git history keeps it forever.
#
# Every file in this folder is a live download at slatedictation.com/<name>.
# Only builds that ask for a key (2.3.0 and later) belong here. The free
# builds before them (1.1.0 to 2.2.0) never ask for one, so anyone could use
# them free for good; the owner had them taken down on 2026-11-14, replacing
# the 2026-09-24 decision to keep them. They remain in git history. Never put
# one back, and never list one in appcast.xml.
